# ShipCES daily delivery report. Generated by Claude Code.
#
# Install on the VPS as: /etc/cron.d/shipces-scrum  (root:root, mode 644, LF line endings)
#
# The job delegates to /opt/shipces-scrum/run-shipces-scrum.sh rather than
# inlining a `cp && cp && exec` chain here. History: the inline chain read its
# source files from /opt/colaberry-accelerator/cron/, which sits inside the
# accelerator deploy tree and was wiped twice by compose/repo rewrites (Jul 12,
# and again around Jul 22). Each time, the `cp` failed, the `&&` chain
# short-circuited, and the report silently stopped sending with nothing in the
# log. The Jul 22 breakage went unnoticed for 13 business days.
#
# The wrapper fixes both halves of that: its source directory lives OUTSIDE the
# deploy tree, and every precondition failure writes a timestamped FAIL line.
#
# Health check: `tail /var/log/shipces-scrum.log` should show a START and a
# DONE line each weekday morning. A FAIL line names exactly what is missing.
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
CRON_TZ=America/Chicago
55 7 * * 1-5 root /opt/shipces-scrum/run-shipces-scrum.sh
